WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500 line:10%
- Joining us now from Baltimore,

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.370 line:10%
Dr. Tom Inglesby, Director

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.170 line:10%
of the Center

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.330 line:10%
for Health Security at Johns

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.530 line:10%
Hopkins University.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.150 line:10%
Doctor, I know you watched

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:10.350 line:10%
the rally last night

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.680 line:10%
from a public health standpoint,

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.260 line:10%
if not a political one.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.100 line:10%
I guess the good news

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.360 line:10%
was there wasn't as big

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.680 line:10%
a crowd as expected.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.200 line:10%
But as an epidemiologist

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.040 line:10%
watching that rally last night,

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.650 line:10%
what did you see?

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.740 line:10%
 Yeah, I thought that the rally

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.330 line:10%
was concerning in terms

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.860 line:10%
of public health risk.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.690 line:10%
I mean, CDC's recent guidance

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.210 line:10%
was that the highest risk

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.440 line:10%
gatherings are those that are

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.840 line:10%
large, indoors, where people

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.220 line:10%
can't stay apart

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.330 line:10%
from each other more than six

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.470 line:10%
feet, and where people travel

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:42.270 line:10%
from out of town.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.620 line:10%
And this rally met all

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.100 line:10%
of those criteria.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.530 line:10%
And what I saw was that people

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.850 line:10%
were sitting quite close

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.440 line:10%
to each other, didn't see very

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.420 line:10%
many people wearing masks.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.560 line:10%
There were some people

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.850 line:10%
handshaking without hand

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.760 line:10%
sanitizer, lots of shouting.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:56.700 line:10%
All of those things

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.900 line:10%
will increase the risk

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.068 line:10%
of spread.

00:01:00.068 --> 00:01:00.940 line:10%
CHRIS WALLACE: Given all

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.620 line:10%
of that, does the president's

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:03.910 line:10%
rally in Tulsa

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:05.379 line:10%
have the potential

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:06.700 line:10%
to be a super spreader

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.400 line:10%
of the virus?

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.050 line:10%
 We have seen

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.380 line:10%
in the past few months

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.180 line:10%
around the world

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.520 line:10%
that indoor gatherings have been

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:16.900 line:10%
the source of most

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.100 line:10%
super spreading events.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.780 line:10%
And those are events where one

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:21.250 line:10%
person can give it to--

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.690 line:10%
give the virus to many people,

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:23.740 line:10%
so there's an opportunity

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.510 line:10%
for much more spread

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:26.840 line:10%
in a short period of time.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.630 line:10%
So I am worried about that.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:29.500 line:10%
I know that many people

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:30.500 line:10%
in the public health community

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.050 line:10%
are worried about the potential

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.630 line:10%
for a big spreading event.

00:01:36.294 --> 00:01:37.740 line:10%
 I want to pick up on that

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:38.670 line:10%
because a number

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:39.720 line:10%
of conservatives

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.770 line:10%
point out

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:42.570 line:10%
that a lot of the media,

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.370 line:10%
and even some public health

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.750 line:10%
experts, not you, but some

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.040 line:10%
of your colleagues

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.590 line:10%
didn't express the same concerns

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.330 line:10%
when there were tens

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:52.170 line:10%
of thousands

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.960 line:10%
of people taking to the streets

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.040 line:10%
in protests

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.210 line:10%
over the death of George

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.980 line:10%
Floyd, many of them

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:00.390 line:10%
not wearing masks.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.330 line:10%
Is-- is there some hypocrisy

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.310 line:10%
where public health concerns

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.860 line:10%
depend upon the politics

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:08.910 line:10%
of the gathering that's being

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.716 line:10%
held?

00:02:10.716 --> 00:02:13.050 line:10%
 Well, they shouldn't depend

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:14.260 line:10%
on the gathering that's being

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.060 line:10%
held.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:15.893 line:10%
I think the public health

00:02:15.893 --> 00:02:17.580 line:10%
principles are the same

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.110 line:10%
whether it's for one purpose

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.130 line:10%
or another.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.810 line:10%
I certainly sympathize

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.850 line:10%
with the motivations of the--

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:24.810 line:10%
the demonstrations that have

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.790 line:10%
gone on across the country,

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.560 line:10%
but I do worry that they are

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.370 line:10%
an opportunity for spread.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:31.410 line:10%
I think it's a little bit--

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:33.060 line:10%
it were even more than a little

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.200 line:10%
bit different than having

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.000 line:10%
a large indoor gathering.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.530 line:10%
We know that outdoor risks are

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.280 line:10%
less than indoor risks.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.370 line:10%
And if people can maintain

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.150 line:10%
their space, then that will

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:43.950 line:10%
help.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:45.370 line:10%
But certainly, I think there is

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.170 line:10%
a risk

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.330 line:10%
with large-scale protesting,

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.201 line:10%
as well, for increased spread.

00:02:51.201 --> 00:02:53.400 line:10%
 Let me ask you about that

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.860 line:10%
because there has been some

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.900 line:10%
testing of protesters after

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.700 line:10%
the big-- after the big events

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.250 line:10%
in Minneapolis and New York.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.810 line:10%
And at least so far,

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.160 line:10%
and I understand the incubation

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.510 line:10%
period goes on, there has not

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.960 line:10%
been any clear spike detected

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.970 line:10%
as a result of those.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:12.930 line:10%
Is it possible

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.850 line:10%
that public health experts are

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.950 line:10%
exaggerating the risk

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.530 line:10%
from these big public

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.295 line:10%
gatherings?

00:03:22.295 --> 00:03:23.320 line:10%
 I don't think they're

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.430 line:10%
exaggerating the risks.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.860 line:10%
I do think, again, that

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.610 line:10%
it's-- we know from what

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:28.720 line:10%
we've seen so far in the last

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.970 line:10%
few months that outdoors is less

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:33.490 line:10%
of a risk than indoors and that

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:35.890 line:10%
mask use has a major impact.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:37.030 line:10%
So to the extent that people are

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:37.730 line:10%
wearing masks

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:38.597 line:10%
in a particular gathering,

00:03:38.597 --> 00:03:40.940 line:10%
that will help a lot.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.100 line:10%
And it is also a little bit

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.860 line:10%
too soon to say whether or not

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:45.730 line:10%
the protests have led

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.170 line:10%
to increased cases, although I

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:48.130 line:10%
am very glad to see

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:50.620 line:10%
that the initial studies do show

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.630 line:10%
that there doesn't seem to be

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.170 line:10%
an increased rate of spread.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:54.970 line:10%
It's quite

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:56.930 line:10%
different in an indoor setting

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:57.730 line:10%
where people are sitting

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:58.530 line:10%
shoulder to shoulder

00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:59.590 line:10%
for a prolonged period of time

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:00.850 line:10%
and really in close quarters

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:02.974 line:10%
like that.

00:04:02.974 --> 00:04:05.200 line:10%
 Every time you come on,

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.480 line:10%
I ask you where are we

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.430 line:10%
with the coronavirus cases.

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.530 line:90%
And I want to put up a map that

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:13.240 line:90%
shows the fact that while there

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.010 line:90%
are significant decreases

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:15.940 line:90%
in a lot of the places

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.779 line:90%
that were hit earliest

00:04:17.779 --> 00:04:18.579 line:90%
and hardest,

00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:19.379 line:90%
there are now

00:04:19.379 --> 00:04:21.010 line:90%
21 states in the West

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:23.020 line:90%
and in the South that are seeing

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.720 line:90%
at least a 25% increase

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.430 line:90%
in new cases.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.320 line:10%
Dr. Inglesby, how much of that

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.760 line:10%
do you think is just the fact

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.190 line:10%
that we're testing more people?

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.380 line:10%
How much of that do you think

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.510 line:10%
is the fact that maybe we're

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:38.330 line:10%
reopening too soon?

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:39.130 line:10%
And how much

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.260 line:10%
of that do you think is--

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.350 line:10%
that there is, in fact,

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:43.150 line:10%
a spread,

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:44.450 line:10%
a spike in the virus in some

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.250 line:10%
of these states

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.870 line:10%
where there has been reopening?

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.860 line:10%
 I think it's a combination

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:54.660 line:10%
of more testing and a real--

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.230 line:10%
an important spike,

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.190 line:10%
in many cases,

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.210 line:10%
in many-- many states

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.440 line:10%
across the country.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.630 line:10%
And you can distinguish what

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.040 line:10%
is more testing from what

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.080 line:10%
is more serious disease

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.520 line:10%
from looking at hospitalization

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.950 line:10%
rate, ICU rate, and the percent

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.560 line:10%
positivity of the overall tests

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:12.970 line:10%
in a given state.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:14.590 line:10%
And in many states, in the ones

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:15.670 line:10%
that you just showed,

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.260 line:10%
particularly Arizona, Texas,

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.970 line:10%
the Carolinas, Florida, what

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:20.770 line:10%
we're seeing

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:22.450 line:10%
is increased positivity,

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.370 line:10%
and testing, and, in many cases,

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:25.730 line:10%
increased hospitalizations,

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:27.640 line:10%
so serious illness happening.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.590 line:10%
That's not just because we're

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:30.920 line:10%
doing more testing in a state.

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:31.990 line:10%
That's because there is more

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.220 line:10%
serious disease in a state.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:35.020 line:10%
So that's a rise.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:35.404 line:10%
 And do you think some

00:05:35.404 --> 00:05:35.580 line:10%
of those--

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:36.020 line:10%
 That's a real rise

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:36.580 line:10%
and [INAUDIBLE]

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:37.380 line:10%
 Do you think some

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.420 line:10%
of those states, Doctor,

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.220 line:10%
should--

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:40.120 line:10%
should pull back on

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.960 line:10%
the reopening, should-- should,

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:42.760 line:10%
you know,

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:43.600 line:10%
if they're in phase two,

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:44.740 line:10%
go back to phase one,

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.640 line:10%
or even go back

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:49.570 line:10%
into partial lockdowns?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:52.420 line:10%
 I don't think we need to go

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:54.950 line:10%
into lockdown in these places

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:55.750 line:10%
at this point.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.710 line:10%
I think each state has

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:58.510 line:10%
a different story.

00:05:58.510 --> 00:05:59.980 line:10%
Each state has its own reopening

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:01.030 line:10%
process, and they're all

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.290 line:10%
slightly different.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:03.970 line:10%
I do think that governors should

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.310 line:10%
be guiding their-- their public

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.810 line:10%
to avoid large gatherings, where

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:09.640 line:10%
we see the greatest

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.260 line:10%
potential risk.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.250 line:10%
They should also be really

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:13.690 line:10%
strongly encouraging people--

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:14.800 line:10%
leaders should be encouraging

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.270 line:10%
people to use the tools that we

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.427 line:10%
know work.

00:06:17.427 --> 00:06:18.460 line:10%
We should be encouraging people

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:19.630 line:10%
to wear face coverings,

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:21.100 line:10%
to stay at a distance,

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.450 line:10%
to avoid large gatherings,

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.100 line:10%
to use hand sanitizer

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.027 line:10%
or wash your hands.

00:06:25.027 --> 00:06:25.960 line:10%
I mean, those are the things

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.730 line:10%
that we know work, and leaders

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:28.540 line:10%
really should, I think,

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:29.950 line:10%
double down in communicating

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.837 line:10%
that across the country.

00:06:31.837 --> 00:06:32.770 line:10%
Those are the things that we

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:35.731 line:10%
have seen work and will work.

00:06:35.731 --> 00:06:38.110 line:10%
 President Trump talked

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:41.350 line:10%
this week about the virus,

00:06:41.350 --> 00:06:42.340 line:10%
the spread of the virus

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.140 line:10%
and also

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:44.200 line:10%
about medical treatments.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:45.690 line:10%
Here he is on that.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:46.490 line:10%
DONALD TRUMP: We're very

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:47.430 line:10%
close to a vaccine,

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:48.230 line:10%
and we're very

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:50.720 line:10%
close to therapeutics, really

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:51.770 line:10%
good therapeutics.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:53.930 line:10%
And but even without that--

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:54.830 line:10%
I don't even like to talk

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.910 line:10%
about that because it's fading

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:57.710 line:10%
away.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:00.776 line:10%
It's going to fade away.

00:07:00.776 --> 00:07:03.300 line:10%
 Is the coronavirus fading

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.100 line:10%
away?

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.380 line:10%
Are we close, very close,

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.030 line:10%
to a vaccine?

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.290 line:10%
And the World Health

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:11.090 line:10%
Organization said this week

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:12.450 line:10%
that we are in a-- let me get it

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:13.250 line:10%
right--

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.740 line:10%
"a new and dangerous phase"

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:16.760 line:10%
of COVID-19.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.610 line:10%
Best case, best case, how long

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:20.750 line:10%
are we going to be living

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:24.646 line:10%
and dealing with this virus?

00:07:24.646 --> 00:07:26.630 line:10%
 Well, the first thing to say

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.010 line:10%
is it's not fading away.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.080 line:10%
The US has more cases than it's

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.190 line:10%
had in many, many weeks.

00:07:34.190 --> 00:07:35.330 line:10%
If you compare us to other parts

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.080 line:10%
of the world, our numbers

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:37.880 line:10%
are on the rise.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:40.250 line:10%
The European Union-- last--

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.370 line:10%
last week, we had 25,000 cases

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.170 line:10%
in a particular day,

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:44.980 line:10%
and the European Union had 4,000

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:45.950 line:10%
cases.

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:47.220 line:10%
So it's not fading away

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:48.020 line:10%
in the US.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:48.860 line:10%
It's not fading away

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:49.560 line:10%
in the world.

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:50.560 line:10%
There's something on the order

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:51.620 line:10%
of 70 or 80 countries

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:53.220 line:10%
where the virus is on the rise.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.020 line:10%
So it's

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:55.950 line:10%
a serious, serious pandemic.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:56.960 line:10%
And as the WHO said,

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:58.040 line:10%
we are in a new phase

00:07:58.040 --> 00:07:59.360 line:10%
of intensity in many parts

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:00.590 line:10%
of the world.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:03.260 line:10%
Vaccine development is going

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:04.430 line:10%
as quickly as it's ever gone

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.490 line:10%
for any vaccine in the world.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:06.290 line:10%
And there are a couple

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:07.250 line:10%
of vaccine trials

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:08.480 line:10%
that are really ramping up

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:09.900 line:10%
in the next month.

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:10.970 line:10%
So that's all good news.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:12.290 line:10%
But we don't know yet

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:13.710 line:10%
whether and when that vaccine

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:14.510 line:10%
will work.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:15.740 line:10%
We hope we'll have vaccine

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:16.630 line:10%
by the end of this year,

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:17.630 line:10%
but I don't think we can count

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:18.800 line:10%
on it yet.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:19.850 line:10%
So I think people really need

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.410 line:10%
to focus on what they can do

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:22.910 line:10%
to decrease transmission

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.740 line:10%
while we wait for a vaccine

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.120 line:10%
and continue to do

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.530 line:10%
the things that we know work

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:30.422 line:10%
in terms of preventing spread.

00:08:30.422 --> 00:08:32.400 line:10%
 Dr. Inglesby, thank you.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.200 line:10%
Thanks for your time

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.070 line:10%
on this Father's Day.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:36.339 line:10%
Always good to talk with, sir.

